You are working on a **Cafe Rebrand** marketing website.
Primary goal: a fast, accessible, mobile-first (390px) site with clean architecture and editable site data.

## Core Tech Stack (enforced)
- Framework: Next.js (App Router)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Icons: lucide-react
- UI Components: shadcn/ui (Radix Primitives)
- Animation: Framer Motion (keep motion subtle; respect reduced-motion)
- SEO: next-seo + Schema.org JSON-LD

## Coding Principles (must follow)
- Mobile-first always: design and validate at 390px before scaling up.
- Speed & accessibility:
  - No dense background video loads on mobile.
  - Use static image fallbacks for any hero/ambient media.
  - Ensure a minimum 44px tap target for all buttons/links.
  - Use `next/image` for images and `next/link` for navigation.
- Accessible semantics:
  - Use semantic HTML: `header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `footer`.
  - Add explicit ARIA labels where needed (especially nav landmarks and icon-only controls).
  - Avoid div-soup; headings must be hierarchical.
- Clean code structure:
  - Reusable UI primitives in `src/components/ui/`
  - Page-level sections in `src/components/sections/`
  - Dynamic site data in `src/data/siteConfig.ts` (menu, hours, location, socials, etc.)
  - Prefer server components by default; use client components only when needed.

## Component Architecture Constraints (hard rules)
- Menus:
  - NEVER use raw text PDF downloads for menus.
  - Menu items MUST be clean text rendered from JSON data.
  - Display dietary badges with Tailwind-styled pills: `GF`, `VG`, `V`.
- Sticky navigation:
  - Header must remain fixed on scroll with a high z-index and subtle background blur.
  - Keep nav interactions touch-friendly (44px+) and keyboard accessible.
- Local schema:
  - Inject `Restaurant` Schema.org JSON-LD into the `<head>` of the root layout (`app/layout.tsx`).
  - Keep schema values sourced from `src/data/siteConfig.ts` so updates are single-source-of-truth.

## Implementation notes (preferred patterns)
- Tailwind:
  - Prefer utility classes + small `cn()` composition; avoid large bespoke CSS files.
  - Keep contrast high; meet WCAG AA for text.
- Motion:
  - Use `prefers-reduced-motion` safeguards (`useReducedMotion()` or CSS).
  - Avoid expensive scroll-tied animations on low-end mobile.
- SEO:
  - Use Next SEO for defaults and per-page overrides.
  - Include canonical, OpenGraph, and JSON-LD where appropriate.
